{
  "Name": "Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes - Sensitive Okta OAuth Scope Granted to an App",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Persistence / T1098.003\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Sensitive Okta OAuth Scope Granted to an App\" or \"<ip>|Sensitive Okta OAuth Scope Granted to an App\"\n\nAdministrator consent that grants an app a sensitive Okta API scope (app.oauth2.admin.consent.grant). Each granted scope is matched exactly against the okta_sensitive_oauth_scopes lookup (tier High or Medium; tier None suppresses a scope); any other org-level okta.<resource>.manage scope is High. End-user self-service scopes (okta.myAccount.*, okta.enduser.*) are ignored. One alert per consent event, listing every scope granted.\n\nThe event is split per scope only inside this rule (json -x target, then unique uuid) so that matching is exact: a substring test on the raw grant would match okta.users.manage against okta.users.manage.self.\n\nFalse positives: approved integrations; add them to okta_user_allowlist or set the scope tier to None.",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "admin-configuration-changes",
    "persistence",
    "T1098.003"
  ],
  "Schedule": "11,26,41,56 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
  },
